# Build output
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Each crate under crates/net is its own workspace root, excluded from this one
# so that upstream's tests and lints do not run as part of ours. That means
# building any of them by hand drops a `target/` beside its manifest, which the
# anchored rule above does not reach. Their lock files are artifacts too: they
# build libraries, not binaries, and none of them is tracked.
crates/net/*/target/
crates/net/*/Cargo.lock

# --- Secrets and personal data -----------------------------------------------
#
# These are the files that must never reach a repository. An identity key is
# the identity: there is no recovery and no revocation authority, so a key that
# lands in a commit is compromised permanently and stays compromised in the
# history even after the file is deleted.
#
# Invitations are capabilities. A blocklist is a list of people somebody chose
# to avoid, which is personal information about them and about the user.

*.key
*.invites
*.blocks
rotelyx-identity.*
*.allow

# Swap files created for local testing
/swapfile*

# --- The operator's own addresses --------------------------------------------
#
# The committed deployment notes use RELAY_HOST and NGINX_HOST as placeholders.
# The real LAN addresses go in a `.local.md` beside them, which stays here.
# A public hostname is in DNS and reveals nothing; a private address reveals the
# shape of somebody's network.

docs/*.local.md
docs/*.local.conf

# --- Test audio ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The speech clips the codec is measured on are 2.3 MB of binary that git would
# carry in its history for ever, and they are regenerable: `scripts/make-speech`
# rebuilds them from a text-to-speech model. The measurements skip themselves
# when the clips are absent rather than failing, so a fresh clone still builds
# and still passes.

crates/rotelyx-codec/tests/speech/
target/listening/

# --- Editor and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ------------------------------------------------
#
# crates/net/ holds the vendored transport, 121,000 lines of source. It is
# committed on purpose: it is what makes a fresh clone build without fetching
# anything from a third party registry. Do not add it here.
#
# Cargo.lock is committed because this workspace produces binaries. It is what
# pins the resolved graph so a clone gets the same dependencies.

# The public site. Served from elsewhere; it is not part of the source tree.
/site/

# Kept out of the public repository. Notes on access, tiers and billing live
# here and are not part of what is published.
/private/

# Fuzzing. The corpus and the artifacts are machine-specific and grow without
# bound; the targets and the manifest are not. A case that found something
# belongs in the ordinary test suite as a regression, where it runs on every
# change, rather than in a corpus somebody has to remember to replay.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/target/

# Python leaves these beside any module it imports, and the version in the name
# changes with the interpreter, so name the directory rather than the file.
__pycache__/
